From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ImpulseROM <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Enable FW_SUPPORT_MULTI_RESOLUTION, FW_MULTI_RESOLUTION_POLICY and FW_DYNAMIC_RESOLUTION_CONTROL

One UI 8.5 (S721B DZF3) compiles CoreRune multi resolution flags to false (v4).
Store the constant true (v3) for FW_SUPPORT_MULTI_RESOLUTION, FW_MULTI_RESOLUTION_POLICY,
and FW_DYNAMIC_RESOLUTION_CONTROL so the dynamic resolution control code in services.jar
(WindowManagerService, LocalDisplayAdapter, DisplayContent, LogicalDisplayMapper) is active.
This ensures physical DPI (xdpi/ydpi) is properly scaled when running at FHD+ and HD+,
preventing fingerprint sensor alignment and status bar offset issues on multi-resolution devices.
---
 smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune.smali | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune.smali
+++ b/smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune.smali
@@ -2783,11 +2783,11 @@
     :goto_a
     sput-boolean v0, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_TSP_DEADZONE_LARGE_FLIP_COVER:Z
 
-    sput-boolean v4, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_SUPPORT_MULTI_RESOLUTION:Z
-
-    sput-boolean v4, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_MULTI_RESOLUTION_POLICY:Z
-
-    sput-boolean v4, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_DYNAMIC_RESOLUTION_CONTROL:Z
+    sput-boolean v3, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_SUPPORT_MULTI_RESOLUTION:Z
+
+    sput-boolean v3, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_MULTI_RESOLUTION_POLICY:Z
+
+    sput-boolean v3, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_DYNAMIC_RESOLUTION_CONTROL:Z
 
     const-string v0, "1"
 
